Why the copyright notices are here and not in LICENSE
-----------------------------------------------------
The LICENSE file is kept byte-for-byte identical to the official GPL-3.0 text
published by the Free Software Foundation, which states that the license
document itself may be copied but not changed. GitHub identifies GPL-3.0 by
matching that file exactly, so adding a copyright line to it makes the
repository lose its GPL-3.0 label and fall back to "Other". The copyright
notices therefore live in this file instead.

Because Dynamic Notch is a derivative work of Boring Notch, it inherits the
GPL-3.0 license and cannot be relicensed under different terms. Anyone
distributing Dynamic Notch, modified or not, must pass on the same freedoms
and make the corresponding source available.

